"""Micras wall sensor: an SFH 4550 IR LED stacked over a TPS601A phototransistor, through-hole.

A custom part: the two leaded devices are bent 90 degrees to lie flat and look
forward over the board edge, the LED (pads 1-2) above the phototransistor
(pads 3-4). Footprint and STEP (WALL_SENSOR_STACKED) from the Altium MicrasLib.

Pins (pad = symbol pin):
| Pad | Pin | Device |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | LED_A | SFH 4550 anode |
| 2 | LED_K | SFH 4550 cathode (the package's marked lead, SFH-DS p.10) |
| 3 | PT_C | TPS601A collector (pin 2 of the TPS601A) |
| 4 | PT_E | TPS601A emitter (pin 1 of the TPS601A) |

The footprint's pad numbers are not the manufacturers' lead numbers: the SFH
4550 recommended solder pad calls the cathode "Pad 1" (SFH-DS p.11), and the
TPS601A numbers its emitter 1 and collector 2 (TPS-DS p.1, "Pin Connection").
Fit each lead to the pad named above.

SFH 4550, 850 nm IR emitter, radial T1 3/4 (ams-OSRAM SFH 4550 datasheet
Version 1.9, 2022-08-09, "SFH-DS"):
- Maximum ratings (p.4): IF 100 mA DC; IF pulse 1 A at tp <= 400 us, D <= 0.005;
  VR 5 V; Ptot 180 mW; Tj 100 C; -40 to +100 C operating.
- Characteristics (p.5): VF 1.5 V typ, 1.7 V max at 100 mA (tp = 20 ms);
  2.4 V typ, 2.9 V max at 1 A (tp = 100 us); half angle +/-3 deg;
  tr = tf = 12 ns; RthJA 450 K/W.
- Pulse handling: "Permissible Pulse Handling Capability" chart (p.8) gives the
  allowed pulse current against tp and duty cycle.

TPS601A(F), NPN phototransistor, TO-18 metal can (Toshiba TPS601A(F) datasheet,
2004-02-06, "TPS-DS"):
- Maximum ratings (p.1): VCEO 40 V, VECO 5 V, IC 50 mA, PC 150 mW
  (-1.2 mW/C above 25 C), -40 to +125 C operating.
- Characteristics (p.2): light current IL at VCE = 3 V, E = 0.1 mW/cm2:
  100 uA min (no rank), A 100-300 uA, B 200-600 uA, C 400-1200 uA;
  VCE(sat) 0.4 V max at IC = 30 uA; tr = tf = 2 us typ at VCC = 5 V,
  IC = 10 mA, RL = 100 ohm; peak sensitivity 800 nm; half angle +/-10 deg.
- Lead forming (p.2, Precaution 2): bend at least 2 mm from the body, before
  soldering.

The emitter series resistor, the LED switch and the phototransistor load belong
to the board circuit.

Sourcing: the parts are bought separately (SFH 4550 from ams-OSRAM, TPS601A(F)
from Toshiba) and hand-soldered after the leads are formed, so the component is
excluded from the JLCPCB BOM and placement file (skip_bom). Each fitted sensor
takes one SFH 4550 and one TPS601A(F).
"""

LED_A = io(Net)
LED_K = io(Net)
PT_C = io(Net)
PT_E = io(Net)

Component(
    name="WALL",
    prefix="W",
    symbol=Symbol(library="WallSensor.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("WallSensor_SFH4550_TPS601A_THT.kicad_mod"),
    pins={
        "LED_A": LED_A,
        "LED_K": LED_K,
        "PT_C": PT_C,
        "PT_E": PT_E,
    },
    properties={
        "emitter": "SFH 4550 (ams-OSRAM)",
        "detector": "TPS601A(F) (Toshiba)",
        "assembly": "hand-soldered, leads formed",
    },
    skip_bom=True,
)
